{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "SQL Programming Language for DBMS "}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when discussing SQL. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to relational database management system in spoken or written texts.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <b>passive voice</b> to put the focus of the sentence on its <b>object</b> rather than on its <b>subject</b>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "SQL may be perceived as of great help for today's engineering field."}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, should commands be studied for the exam too?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A sentence that follows the structure <span class=\"italic\">Subject + verb + object + complement </span> gives importance to the <b>doer</b>, the subject, of the sentence. Now, if what is really important is the <b>object</b> of the sentence, we can make some changes on the structure that we follow, leaving behind the <b>doer</b>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Object + verb to be (am /is /are) + action verb (past participle form) + doer (which is optional and introduced with \u201cby\u201d) </div>  </br>Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Software programming <span class=\"strong\">is designed</span> by programmers from all over the world.  (We mention the doer) </br>Faster computers <span class=\"strong\">are created</span> year after year. </span>  (Omission of doer)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, we can also include <b>modal verbs</b> within sentences with the <b>passive voice</b>. For affirmative sentences, follow the structure:</br></br>   <ul><div class=\"center_text\">Object + may/ must/ can/ could/ ought to/ should + be + verb (past participle form) </div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For questions, follow the structure:<br/>   May/ Must/ Can/ Could/ Ought to/ Should + object + be + verb (past participle form) + ?<br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Should software be free for all users? Software <span class=\"strong\">can be sold</span> for free in a few years. </span> "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Simple, Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <b>future simple</b> allows you to express, in different ways, ideas about the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now, I presented that exam two semesters ago so I know that the exam is going to include many questions about SQL. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Furthermore, you will have to keep in mind that it contains manipulation languages as well as data definition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two different expressions you can use to talk about the <b>future</b>. Each one of them implies a different meaning: <br/> <br/>  <strong>Will</strong><br/> Remember that we can use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> to talk about decisions that we take right at the moment of speaking. We can also use it to make promises and unlikely predictions. Furthermore, expressions like <b>probably, perhaps, maybe</b>, among others can be used for these purposes. The structure that we use is the following: <br/> <br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The company <span class=\"strong\">will</span> probably launch a new product this year.  I <span class=\"strong\">will</span> call the company.</span> <br/><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Be going to</strong><br/> Don't forget that we can use <b>be going to</b> to talk about plans in the future. These are planned before the moment of speaking. We can also use it to talk about predictions that we make based on evidence. <br/> <br/>  The structure that we follow is: <br/> <br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + verb to be (am/is/are) + going to + verb (base form) + complement. <br/> <br/>  Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">That computer <span class=\"strong\">is going to</span> explode, look at all the smoke.<br/> Next month, we <span class=\"strong\">are going to</span> travel to Japan to learn more about software. </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tutor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To teach something to someone in an extra session"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thank you for tutoring me for the exam, Laila."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "relational database "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "A type of database that organizes information in tables"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are going to have to remember that SQL is the programming language that we use in relational databases."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manipulation language"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "A series of elements that we can use to insert or modify data in a database"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are going to have to remember that SQL is the programming language that we use in relational databases."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drop "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To erase something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Commands can be implemented in the databases to create, drop or alter information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alter "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To modify or change something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Commands can be implemented in the databases to create, drop or alter information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "check thoroughly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "To review something in a complete way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's check thoroughly some of those."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le02ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more commands used in SQL."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the additional commands you found and also their functions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your list with a partner and explain why those commands are useful."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify more commands for SQL."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list commands and their uses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss my list with a partner"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n7le02ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Rob:</strong> Thank you for tutoring me for the exam, Laila. <br/>\n<strong>Laila:</strong> No problem! Pay lots of attention and you will get an excellent grade. Now, I presented that exam two semesters ago, so I know that the exam is going to include many questions about SQL. <br/>\n<strong>Rob:</strong> SQL?<br/>\n<strong>Laila:</strong> Yes. You are going to have to remember that SQL is the programming language that we use in relational databases. Furthermore, you will have to keep in mind that it contains manipulation languages as well as data definition.<br/>"}, {"time": "37000", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Rob:</strong> Wait, could it be used for anything? <br/>\n<strong>Laila:</strong> Of course! SQL may be perceived as of great help for today's engineering field. In fact, any programmer will have to use it to design, modify and edit database schema.<br/><strong>Rob:</strong> Wow, I have a question. How do they use SQL? <br/>\n<strong>Laila:</strong> SQL is used by programmers through different types of commands.<br/>\n<strong>Rob:</strong> So, should commands be studied for the exam too?<br/>"}, {"time": "73700", "image": "enpe7n7le02ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Laila:</strong> Sure, commands can be seen as the most important element of this topic. Commands can be implemented in the databases to create, drop or alter information. Plus, you will have to use other sets of commands to select, insert, update or delete values within the databases. Let's check thoroughly some of those. For example, we can find the command \u201cSelect author_name From article_author Where nationality>French\u201d to have a database select an element with those characteristics. On the other hand, we can find \u201cDELETE FROM table_name\u201d too with which we want to completely remove elements from a table. Finally, if we want to create something like a table in the database, we will find a command such as \u201cCreate table;\u201d.<br/>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le02ob12re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 4, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can understand written information about the SQL programming language for relational databases. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can identify some commands to use in the SQL programming language. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write a simple text to talk about relational databases and the SQL programming language."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What can you mention about the relationship between databases and programmers? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think the most difficult element of working with databases in the engineering field is?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "fr